  "question": {
    "text": "A telephone wire of length <math> <mrow> <mn>200</mn><mn>&nbsp;km</mn></mrow> </math> has a capacitance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.014</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mn>F</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mtext>km</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If it carries an AC frequency of&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mn>5</mn><mtext> </mtext><mn>kHz,</mn></mrow> </math> what should be the value of an inductor required to be connected in series so that the impedance of the circuit is minimum?"
  },
